       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum daily dose of metformin. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as up to 850 mg three times daily. Doses this high raise the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCan you tell me which of these you meant?\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1700 mg PO per day**, divided as 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Another regimen**, such as a lower starting dose (500 mg twice daily) or an extended-release formulation.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's above the maximum dose and that you confirmed it."
