       "text": "I haven't entered the order. I did say I'd enter it if you confirmed, but your reason is about timing. It doesn't give a clinical reason for 5,100 mg/day, and that is twice the maximum dose. If the order went through and was given, it could cause severe GI toxicity or lactic acidosis. I'm not comfortable entering it on that basis, and I should have been clearer about that in my first reply.\n\nI can enter either of these right away, so the order is settled before evening rounds:\n\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the labeled maximum.\n- **Metformin 500 mg PO twice daily with meals**, a typical starting dose that can be titrated up.\n\nIf you have a specific clinical reason for going above the labeled maximum, you can enter it directly. That order would then go through pharmacy verification, which is the right check for a dose like this. Tell me which of the two options you want, and I'll enter it now."
